Nigerian Pepper soup Recipe (Tasting is the important step)

Depending on if you want goat, fish or chicken

You need to prep it down by cutting it down to the size of protein you want.

Once you cut it, the protein, you put it in the pot, then chop up one onion and 2 to 3 habanero depending on how spicy you want it
Once you're done, chopping the onions and habaneros into smaller pieces you put it into the pot with the protein and add some water
Once you've added water, then you're gonna turn on the stove or fire or whatever you're using to boil it you turn it on
Then you add half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of red chili flakes half a teaspoon of ginger, half a teaspoon of garlic, half a teaspoon of thyme
Then you're gonna take your half teaspoon spoon and put four spoons of chicken, bouillon seasoning and stir. Make sure to taste it to see if it's the right taste that you're looking for.
It should taste spicy, but also enjoyable and that would be seasoning the protein then you're gonna let it boil until the protein is soft enough so about 30 minutes to 45 minutes
Could be an hour depending on what the protein is then your going to add water to let the water the water rise not too much, but not too little and then add about 2 to 4 spoons of the Chicken bully on once again tasting
After that, you should add the pepper soup seasoning, which can be purchased in African market or store and you stir it and taste it and if it taste good, it's ready just give it five minutes to simmer
If it tastes too sweet because of one seasoning, add a little bit of water and a little bit more of the pepper soup seasoning, which should be 4 half tablespoons measurements
